SUMMARY:🍽 Burrito Bowls
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 30 min\n\nStatus unconfirmed — not included in Jul 20 backlog review\n\nRice swapped to a brown/white blend for fiber.\n\nIngredients:\n• 1.0 lb – Member's Mark 80/20 Ground Beef\n• 0.5 lb – Great Value Brown & White Rice Blend\n• 1 can – Rosarita Traditional Refried Beans\n• 1 can – Ro-Tel Diced Tomatoes & Green Chilies\n• 1 packet – McCormick Chili Seasoning Mix
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-07-20-meal@plan.py
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
SUMMARY:🍽 Pasta with RAGU
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 20 min\n\nSides: garlic bread\n\nNo meat — swapped from Sausage & Potato Soup (no Italian sausage on hand). Add garlic bread if still have a loaf.\n\nDouble the sauce and freeze half — saves a future dinner. Use any pasta shape. Great Northern beans pureed into the sauce for hidden fiber. Switched to whole wheat pasta for fiber — sauce masks the flavor/color change.\n\nIngredients:\n• 1.5 lb – 73% Lean / 27% Fat Ground Beef\, 1 lb\n• 1 jar – RAGU Chunky Pasta Sauce\, 24 oz\n• 1 box – Great Value Whole Wheat Linguine\, 16 oz\n• 0.25 jar – Great Value Minced Garlic in Water\, 8 oz\n• 1 pkg – Freshness Guaranteed Garlic Bread\, 16 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Great Northern Beans\, 15.5 oz
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-07-21-meal@plan.py
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260722
SUMMARY:🍽 Mac and Cheese + Hot Dogs
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 20 min\n\nSides: sweet corn\n\nSlice the kielbasa into coins and brown in a pan\, then stir into the mac. Add frozen broccoli to the pasta water. White beans pureed into the cheese sauce for hidden fiber and extra creaminess.\n\nIngredients:\n• 2 box – Kraft Deluxe Mac and Cheese\, 14 oz\n• 1 pkg – Hillshire Farm Polska Kielbasa OR Johnsonville Polish Kielbasa\n• 1 bag – Great Value Frozen Broccoli Florets\, 12 oz\n• 0.25 gal – Great Value Whole Vitamin D Milk\n• 0.25 pkg – Great Value Sweet Cream Salted Butter\n• 1 can – Great Value Great Northern Beans\, 15.5 oz
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-07-22-meal@plan.py
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260723
SUMMARY:🍽 Taco Wednesday — Ground Beef
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 30 min\n\nSides: refried beans / sweet corn\n\nSet up a taco bar — kids love building their own. Black beans pureed into the meat itself\, not just the refried bean side — kids skip the side but eat the meat.\n\nIngredients:\n• 1.5 lb – 73% Lean / 27% Fat Ground Beef\, 1 lb\n• 1 pkg – Old El Paso Stand 'N Stuff Taco Shells OR Flour Tortillas\n• 1 pkt – Great Value Mild Chili Seasoning Mix (as taco seasoning)\, 1 oz\n• 1 can – Old El Paso Traditional Canned Refried Beans\, 16 oz\n• 1 bag – Great Value Fiesta Blend Shredded Cheese\, 8 oz\n• 0.5 tub – Great Value Light Sour Cream\, 16 oz\n• 1 each – Fresh Green Bell Pepper\n• 0.5 each – Fresh Red Onion OR Sweet Onion\n• 2 each – Fresh Lime\n• 1 head – Romaine or Iceberg Lettuce\n• 2 each – Fresh Roma Tomatoes\n• 1 can – Ro-Tel Diced Tomatoes & Green Chilies\n• 1 can – Great Value Black Beans\, 15 oz
END:VEVENT
