UID:2026-09-04-meal@plan.py
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:🍽 Frozen Pizza Night
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 22 min\n\nNew standing Friday rule: Pizza Night\, permanently. Country Fried Steak + Mashed Potatoes (previously slotted here) rolled forward to Sep 13.\n\nKeep 2 in the freezer at all times. Add a bagged salad on the side. Brand notes: MM Rising Crust Four Cheese (cheese night)\, Red Baron preferred for pepperoni (MM pepperoni too salty — confirmed May 22).\n\nIngredients:\n• 2 pkg – Member's Mark Rising Crust Pizza or Red Baron Pepperoni (frozen)\n• 0.5 bag – Great Value Fiesta Blend Shredded Cheese (optional topping)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-05-meal@plan.py
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260906
SUMMARY:🍽 Slow-Cooked Pork Shoulder
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 90 min\n\nSides: Long grain rice or roasted potatoes / bell peppers\n\nNew standing Saturday rule: crockpot meal instead of pizza. Picked for variety vs. Aug 29's carnitas — makes a big roast\, likely yields pulled-pork leftovers. Ingredients not needed on the Aug 29 grocery run (8 days out) — will need their own shopping trip closer to Sep 4-5.\n\n6-10 lb roast — season overnight\, slow-cook all day or oven-roast. Makes pulled pork tacos the next night. Two meals for one cook.\n\nIngredients:\n• 1 roast – Prairie Fresh Natural Pork Shoulder Butt Roast\, Bone-in (~8 lb)\n• 0.5 jar – Great Value Minced Garlic in Water\n• 1 each – Fresh Red Onion\n• 1 bottle – Cholula Cilantro Lime Cremosa Sauce (for serving)\n• 1 side – Great Value Long Grain Rice OR Fresh Russet Potatoes\n• 1 bag – Fresh Produce Whole Color Bell Peppers\, 3 Count
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-05-prep@plan.py
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:🧊 Move pork shoulder to fridge — needs 48h to thaw before cooking
DESCRIPTION:Slow-Cooked Pork Shoulder is in 2 days
END:VEVENT
