SUMMARY:🍽 Beef Chili + Cornbread
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 60 min\n\nSides: Jiffy cornbread\n\nRolled forward from planned Aug 30\, which was swapped same-day for Chicken Legs\, Brown Rice\, and Broccoli Normandy.\n\nMakes great leftovers. JIFFY cornbread muffins bake in 15 min. Double batch and freeze half the chili. Ground flaxseed stirred into the cornbread batter for hidden fiber.\n\nIngredients:\n• 1.5 lb – 73% Lean / 27% Fat Ground Beef\, 1 lb\n• 3 can – Great Value Light Red Kidney Beans\, 15.5 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Pinto Beans\, 15.5 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Crushed Tomatoes with Tomato Puree\, 28 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Tomato Paste\, 6 oz\n• 2 pkt – Great Value Mild Chili Seasoning Mix\, 1 oz\n• 2 box – "JIFFY" Corn Muffin Mix\, 8.5 oz\n• 0.25 carton – Great Value Large White Eggs\, 18 ct (for cornbread)\n• 0.25 gal – Great Value Whole Vitamin D Milk (for cornbread)\n• 1 bag – Great Value Fiesta Blend Shredded Cheese\, 8 oz\n• 0.5 tub – Great Value Light Sour Cream\, 16 oz\n• 0.1 bag – Great Value Ground Flaxseed\, 12 oz
